{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":2,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make the refresh engine test assert that the manifest passed to signing.sign_manifest contains `engine: agentic`, instead of replacing build_manifest and checking its `fields` argument","criteria":["tests"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["monkeypatch.setattr(attest, \"build_manifest\", _capture)","assert built[\"coverage\"][\"engine\"] == \"agentic\"","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py:304: \"engine\": manifest_engine(prior_manifest),","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py:322: manifest = build_manifest(","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py:348: return signing.sign_manifest(ticket_id, manifest, kind=_MANIFEST_PREFIX, repo_root=repo_root)","The observable contract in the commit message is that drift refresh carries the engine from the prior manifest into the signed bytes. The test only checks a dict passed between two internal functions.","assert attest.manifest_engine is manifest.manifest_engine","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py:9: # Re-export manifest helpers so historical ``attest.<name>`` imports remain stable.","manifest_engine is added in this diff (`+def manifest_engine(` in manifest.py), so no historical caller imports it from attest"],"finding":"test_refresh_carries_the_prior_engine monkeypatches attest.build_manifest, which is internal to the unit under test, and asserts on the intermediate `fields` dict (`built[\"coverage\"][\"engine\"]`). It never checks the manifest the refresh actually signs, so it fails on a refactor that keeps behavior, and it cannot catch a regression where build_manifest drops the carried engine on the refresh path.","id":"0","impact":0.0,"location":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_engine.py","merged_from":["`assert attest.manifest_engine is manifest.manifest_engine` checks only that a re-export points at the same object. manifest_engine is new in this diff, so no historical `attest.manifest_engine` import exists for the compatibility re-export to protect. The assertion pins module layout, not behavior."],"norm_id":"nb58c11455671a2d4","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","reviewer_id":"code-review-tests","reviewers":["code-review-tests"],"scenarios":["refresh_attestation passes the engine as a build_manifest kwarg instead of inside coverage: the signed output is the same, but the test fails","build_manifest's `if engine in _SIGNED_ENGINES` path regresses only for refreshes: the test still passes because build_manifest is replaced"],"suggested_fix":"Leave build_manifest real. Monkeypatch `signing.sign_manifest` (the signing boundary) to capture its `manifest` argument, then assert `\"engine: agentic\" in captured_manifest`. Optionally add a second case with a prior manifest that has no engine line and assert that no `engine:` line is written.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5714,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"local","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"low","escapes_automation":false,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":false,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reachable_path_without_auto